  "description": "XOPPID crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P -3 1 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: Na1 1+,C248 H168 Ce13 N54 O60 5+,6(N1 O3 1-),20(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 12 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce10 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce11 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce12 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce13 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 33 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.323-5.185 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 115.79-167.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Na[Ce13(ccnm)6(CO3)14(H2O)6(phen)18](NO3)6·20H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
